</div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:18pt;margin-top:-6pt;width:264pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Investment
Adviser/Portfolio Managers</font></div> <div style="text-align:left;">
<img src="g108759sharenow_greg.jpg" alt=" " style="height:73pt;width:49pt;"><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;line-height:1pt;margin-left:0%;">&#8201;</font>
<img src="g108759hagedorn_lewis.jpg" alt=" " style="height:72pt;margin-left:0;width:48pt;"><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;line-height:1pt;margin-left:0%;">&#8201;</font>
<img src="g108759dewitt_andrew.jpg" alt=" " style="height:72pt;margin-left:0;width:48pt;"><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;line-height:1pt;margin-left:0%;">&#8201;</font>
<img src="g108759schneider_jerome.jpg" alt=" " style="height:72pt;margin-left:0;width:49pt;"><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;line-height:1pt;margin-left:0%;">&#8201;</font></div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:5pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:5pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">PIMCO serves as the investment adviser for the Fund. The Fund's </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">portfolio is jointly and primarily managed by Greg Sharenow, Lewis </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Hagedorn, Andrew DeWitt and Jerome
Schneider. Messrs. Sharenow </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and Schneider are each Managing Directors of PIMCO. Messrs. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Hagedorn
and DeWitt are each Executive Vice Presidents of PIMCO. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Messrs. Sharenow, Hagedorn, DeWitt and Schneider have managed the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund since its inception in May 2023.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Purchase and Sale of Fund Shares</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund is an exchange-traded fund (&#8220;ETF&#8221;). Individual Fund shares </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">may only be purchased and sold
on a national securities exchange </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">through a broker-dealer and may not be purchased or redeemed directly </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">with the Fund. The price of Fund shares is based on market price, and </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">because ETF shares trade at market
prices rather than net asset value </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">(&#8220;NAV&#8221;), shares may trade at a price greater than NAV (a premium) or </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">less than NAV (a discount). An investor may incur costs attributable to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the difference between the highest
price a buyer is willing to pay to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">purchase shares of the Fund (&#8220;bid&#8221;) and the lowest price a seller is </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">willing to accept for shares (&#8220;ask&#8221;) when buying or selling shares in the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">secondary market (the
&#8220;bid-ask spread&#8221;). Recent information, including </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">information about the Fund&#8217;s NAV, market price, premiums and </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">discounts, and bid-ask spreads, is included on the Fund&#8217;s website at
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">https://www.pimco.com/en-us/investments/etf.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Tax Information</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund&#8217;s distributions are generally taxable to you as ordinary income, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">capital gains, or a
combination of the two, unless you are investing </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">through a tax-deferred arrangement, such as a 401(k) plan or an </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">individual retirement account, in which case distributions may be </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">taxable upon withdrawal.</font><font
style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Payments to Broker-Dealers and Other Financial </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Intermediaries</font></div>
</div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">If you purchase Fund shares through a broker-dealer or other financial </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">intermediary, PIMCO or other related companies may pay the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">intermediary for the sale of Fund shares or related
services. These </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">payments may create a conflict of interest by influencing the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">broker-dealer or
other intermediary and your salesperson to recommend </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the Fund over another investment. Ask your salesperson or visit your </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">financial intermediary&#8217;s website for more information.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:0.0pt;text-align:left;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
